DEBUG ONLY -- NOT PART OF ANY BUILD.

Raw-syscall markers through tcc_new, so that a segfault says WHICH STATEMENT
rather than which function. Each exits with a distinct code before any libc
code runs, so nothing can mask it:

    50  reached the field writes at all
    51  s->ppfp = stdout survived
    52  s->include_stack_ptr = s->include_stack survived
    53  tcc_set_lib_path survived, so tcc_new is complete

The probe ladder narrowed the fault to tcc_new and then stopped being useful:
it can only test what can be CALLED, and what is left is a handful of
statements inside one function. Reading the emitted assembly found two real
bugs there (array members loaded rather than decayed, and sized by the wrong
type) and neither was the whole answer -- so this measures instead.

--- a/libtcc.c
+++ b/libtcc.c
@@ -908,11 +908,15 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_NEW_DTAGS
     s->enable_new_dtags = 1;
 #endif
+    asm("mov_x0,50" "mov_x8,93" "svc_0");
     s->ppfp = stdout;
+    asm("mov_x0,51" "mov_x8,93" "svc_0");
     /* might be used in error() before preprocess_start() */
     s->include_stack_ptr = s->include_stack;
+    asm("mov_x0,52" "mov_x8,93" "svc_0");
 
     tcc_set_lib_path(s, CONFIG_TCCDIR);
+    asm("mov_x0,53" "mov_x8,93" "svc_0");
 #ifdef CONFIG_TCC_SWITCHES /* predefined options */
     tcc_set_options(s, CONFIG_TCC_SWITCHES);
 #endif
